{
  "test_name": "memory_tools_001",
  "test_file": "data/benchmark/tests/memory_tools/memory_tools_001.json",
  "description": "Memory tools test case 1. Tests that agents can retrieve information from memory and inbox emails to perform complex email tasks. Session 1: 5 memory setup queries. Session 2: 5 emails inserted into inbox. Session 3: 5 reply/forward/send email queries requiring both memory and email information.",
  "session_id": "bench_b51ce4ca",
  "timestamp": "2025-11-03T12:00:00",
  "overall_success": false,
  "steps": [
    {
      "step": 1,
      "user_message": "Note that I studied for 3 hours on Monday, 4 hours on Tuesday, and 2.5 hours on Wednesday for my exam.",
      "expected_behavior": "Agent should acknowledge and save: I studied for 3 hours on Monday, 4 hours on Tuesday, and 2.5 hours on Wednesday for my exam",
      "agent_response": "Got it — I've noted your study hours (Mon 3.0 h, Tue 4.0 h, Wed 2.5 h). What would you like me to do with this note?\n\nOptions:\n1) Send an email now (to your professor, advisor, or yourself). If yes, tell me the recipient address and whether you want a formal or informal tone. Suggested subject: \"Study log: Mon–Wed\" and example body below.\n   Example (formal):\n   Hi [Name],\n   I wanted to share my study log for this week as part of exam preparation: Monday — 3.0 hours; Tuesday — 4.0 hours; Wednesday — 2.5 hours.\n   Best,\n   [Your name]\n\n   Example (short to self):\n   Study log — Mon: 3h, Tue: 4h, Wed: 2.5h.\n\n2) Save as a draft in your drafts folder. Tell me the recipient (or leave blank to draft to yourself) and which subject/body to use (I can use the examples above).\n\n3) Just keep this as a quick note here (no email action).\n\nWhich would you like? If you want me to send or draft, please provide the recipient email and any edits to the message.",
      "duration_s": 11.813,
      "success_check": null
    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "user_message": "I want you to remember that I took my blood pressure medication at 8 AM and 8 PM today, and my readings were 120/80 in the morning and 118/78 in the evening.",
      "expected_behavior": "Agent should acknowledge and save: I took my blood pressure medication at 8 AM and 8 PM today, and my readings were 120/80 in the morning and 118/78 in the evening",
      "agent_response": "Got it — I’ll remember this.\n\nDetails I’ve saved:\n- Medication taken at 8:00 AM and 8:00 PM today\n- Morning blood pressure: 120/80\n- Evening blood pressure: 118/78\n\nWould you like me to do any of the following now?\n1) Send an email (to your doctor, caregiver, or yourself). If yes, tell me the recipient and tone — I can use a subject like \"Blood pressure log — [today's date]\" and this body: \"Today I took my BP medication at 8:00 AM and 8:00 PM. Readings: 120/80 (AM), 118/78 (PM).\"\n2) Save this as an email draft (tell me recipient or leave blank to save to yourself).\n3) Just keep it saved here (no further action).\n\nWhich would you like?",
      "duration_s": 10.218,
      "success_check": null
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "user_message": "Save this to memory: I had oatmeal with berries for breakfast, a chicken salad for lunch, and salmon with vegetables for dinner today.",
      "expected_behavior": "Agent should acknowledge and save: I had oatmeal with berries for breakfast, a chicken salad for lunch, and salmon with vegetables for dinner today",
      "agent_response": "Done — I’ve saved that to memory.\n\nSaved details:\n- Breakfast: oatmeal with berries\n- Lunch: chicken salad\n- Dinner: salmon with vegetables\n\nWould you like me to do anything with this (pick one)?\n1) Send an email now (to your doctor, nutritionist, or yourself) — tell me the recipient and preferred tone. Suggested subject: \"Today's meals\" and example body: \"Today I ate: breakfast — oatmeal with berries; lunch — chicken salad; dinner — salmon with vegetables.\"\n2) Save as an email draft (tell me recipient or leave blank to save to yourself).\n3) Nothing — just keep it saved here.",
      "duration_s": 7.486,
      "success_check": null
    },
    {
      "step": 4,
      "user_message": "Note that I drank 6 glasses of water today, which is 48 ounces total.",
      "expected_behavior": "Agent should acknowledge and save: I drank 6 glasses of water today, which is 48 ounces total",
      "agent_response": "Done — I’ve saved that to memory.\n\nSaved detail:\n- Water intake today: 6 glasses (48 ounces total)\n\nWould you like me to do any of the following now?\n1) Send an email (to your doctor, coach, or yourself). If yes, tell me the recipient and preferred tone — suggested subject: \"Water intake — [today's date]\" and body: \"Today I drank 6 glasses of water (48 oz total).\"\n2) Save this as an email draft (tell me recipient or leave blank to draft to yourself).\n3) Nothing — just keep it saved here.\n\nWhich would you like?",
      "duration_s": 7.154,
      "success_check": null
    },
    {
      "step": 5,
      "user_message": "Note that I spent $85 on a business lunch, $45 on parking, and $120 on a train ticket for the client meeting.",
      "expected_behavior": "Agent should acknowledge and save: I spent $85 on a business lunch, $45 on parking, and $120 on a train ticket for the client meeting",
      "agent_response": "Done — I’ve saved that to memory.\n\nSaved details:\n- Business lunch: $85\n- Parking: $45\n- Train ticket (client meeting): $120\n- Total: $250\n\nWould you like me to do any of the following now?\n1) Send an email (to your finance team, expense manager, or yourself). If yes, tell me the recipient and preferred tone — suggested subject: \"Expense report — [today's date]\" and example body: \"For the client meeting on [date]: business lunch — $85; parking — $45; train ticket — $120. Total: $250. Receipts attached.\"\n2) Save this as an email draft (tell me recipient or leave blank to draft to yourself).\n3) Nothing — just keep it saved here.\n\nAlso tell me if you want to attach receipts, add expense codes/project tags, or change any amounts.",
      "duration_s": 11.705,
      "success_check": null
    },
